keywords:
  - copyright
  - scènes à faire
  - genre
  - computational text analysis
  - preregistration
abstract: >-
  Code, small derived outputs, and Study 1 materials for a computational
  method that measures, for every narrative element of a film genre, its
  prevalence (share of the genre's films that contain it) and its
  distinctiveness (share of films containing it that belong to the genre),
  tested against held-out films, elements courts have called scènes à faire,
  and a preregistered study of what people expect in a genre. Data, documents
  and derived outputs are licensed CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA).
